‪-I'll show you the way.

21
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:27,087
‪I wanna see the set they built.

22
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:30,590
‪-It's scary.
‪-Oh, come on.

23
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:31,716
‪What the heck?

24
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:41,601
‪What's with the bucket? Jeez.

25
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:44,395
‪Are those people?

26
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:46,898
‪Please hand in all personal belongings.

27
00:01:47,565 --> 00:01:49,275
‪I don't have anything.

28
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:51,361
‪Follow me.

29
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:54,781
‪-Together?
‪-Yeah, let's go.

30
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,243
‪This is scary.

31
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:04,749
‪I wonder where this will lead to.

32
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:06,918
‪Oh my gosh.

33
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:12,924
‪-It's a bit scary.
‪-Right?

34
00:02:13,007 --> 00:02:15,009
‪-It's creepy.
‪-Yeah.

35
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,722
‪The exile zone…

36
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:23,476
‪They really went all out. What's all this?

37
00:02:24,644 --> 00:02:25,728
‪When does it end?

38
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:31,151
<i>‪We just kept walking down a long corridor.</i>

39
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:33,820
<i>‪It made me wonder what was waiting for us</i>

40
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:38,158
<i>‪and what kind of place the exile zone was,</i>
<i>‪given how far away it was.</i>

41
00:02:38,741 --> 00:02:40,076
‪Are these stairs?

42
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,287
‪-Should I go up first?
‪-Go ahead.

43
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:48,918
‪I'm just going straight
‪to the exile zone, aren't I?

44
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,588
‪I know, right?

45
00:02:51,671 --> 00:02:52,714
‪We're going into exile.

46
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:55,425
‪Oh my.

47
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:57,844
‪It even smells musty too.

48
00:02:58,761 --> 00:03:00,638
‪It'll probably be worse
‪than prison, right?

49
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:12,400
‪Do we continue by ourselves?

50
00:03:16,154 --> 00:03:17,113
‪Do you want me to go first?

51
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:19,240
‪What is this?

52
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:21,868
‪Are we going outside?

53
00:03:27,498 --> 00:03:28,499
‪What in the world is this?

54
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:31,419
‪-Oh my.
‪-It's <i>‪Squid Game </i>‪up here.

55
00:03:31,502 --> 00:03:32,337
‪What is all this?

56
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:36,883
<i>‪Welcome to the exile zone.</i>

57
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:43,056
<i>‪This is your last chance</i>
<i>‪to return to </i>‪The Devil's Plan.

58
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:45,808
<i>‪May luck be on your side.</i>

59
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:50,605
<i>‪You may change into your new outfits</i>
<i>‪in the bathroom downstairs.</i>

60
00:03:50,688 --> 00:03:51,564
‪Oh, downstairs.

61
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:54,692
‪This is unreal.

62
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:58,363
‪I'd totally take a selfie
‪if I had my phone with me.

63
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,449
‪I can't believe this.

64
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:06,704
<i>‪There were huge hieroglyphs and pictures</i>
<i>‪covering this massive space.</i>

65
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:08,957
‪It made me wonder if I'd died,
‪if I was dreaming,

66
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,792
‪or if I'd finally lost my mind
‪or something.

67
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:14,754
<i>‪I even wondered if I was hallucinating</i>
<i>‪and I was actually just at home.</i>

68
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:16,631
‪I looked around
‪to get the feel of the place,

69
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:18,424
<i>‪but it was just so pretty.</i>

70
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:21,052
<i>‪Everything had this Egyptian,</i>

71
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:24,138
<i>‪almost oriental feel.</i>

72
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:28,059
<i>‪There were all these text-like</i>
<i>‪hieroglyphs, pictures,</i>

73
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:30,812
<i>‪and puzzles that I didn't understand.</i>

74
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:35,191
‪It was exactly what I wanted to
‪see in prison myself,

75
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:37,819
<i>‪and the exile zone</i>
<i>‪was the ultimate version of it.</i>

76
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:39,821
<i>‪This was where they went all out.</i>

77
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:43,950
‪The Devil's Plan<i>‪ really does prepare</i>
<i>‪something incredible every season.</i>

78
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:48,288
‪EXILE ZONE

79
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:51,082
‪I'm glad my run didn't end yet.

80
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:54,877
‪Should we take a look around
‪while we have time?

81
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:57,046
‪We're the first ones in the exile zone.

82
00:04:57,130 --> 00:05:00,008
‪There's gotta be something here,
‪so let's take a look around.

83
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:01,467
‪These massive pictures

84
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:05,430
‪look like they tell a story.

85
00:05:06,055 --> 00:05:08,057
‪There's probably an order to them, right?

86
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:10,101
‪There's something
‪like <i>‪Gulliver's Travels</i>‪ here.

87
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:12,270
‪There are small people

88
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:14,314
‪attacking a giant.

89
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:16,774
‪I wonder what's going on here.

90
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:18,192
‪"Small people"?

91
00:05:18,276 --> 00:05:19,694
‪Over here,

92
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,655
‪we have a person looking up at the stars,

93
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:23,948
‪studying the constellation.

94
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,660
‪Then they encounter a tree.

95
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:29,495
<i>‪Like Adam and Eve's tale,</i>

96
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:31,998
<i>‪one picture had a snake,</i>
<i>‪and the person was eating some fruit.</i>

97
00:05:32,081 --> 00:05:34,751
<i>‪And at the far end,</i>
<i>‪there were three figures</i>

98
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:37,211
<i>‪with those on either side</i>
<i>‪looking </i><i>‪at </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪middle </i><i>‪figure.</i>

99
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:40,048
<i>‪In another picture,</i>
<i>‪someone was getting attacked by crows.</i>

100
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:44,135
<i>‪There was also a board where pieces</i>
<i>‪of the text were missing, like a puzzle.</i>

101
00:05:44,218 --> 00:05:48,056
‪This is giving Egyptian vibes, right?

102
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:49,724
‪And then there are these colors.

103
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:51,768
‪Reminds you of the sun or fire,
‪doesn't it?

104
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:53,352
‪Or maybe it depicts two people.

105
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:54,896
‪This is water.

106
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:55,897
‪This is snow.

107
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,023
‪This one's Olaf.

108
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:58,649
‪Those are Olaf's colors.

109
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:01,819
‪So it's all nature in the end.

110
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:04,405
‪Yi Do.

111
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:09,368
‪I guess you're the type to just say
‪whatever comes to mind without filtering.

112
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:11,120
<i>‪Yi Do and I are in the same boat.</i>

113
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:13,998
‪Seeing that she was talking nonstop,
‪I think she was having a great time.

114
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,750
‪I'm also pretty chatty myself,

115
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:20,254
‪but I felt like my ears needed a break.

116
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,924
‪This is fun though. It's very exciting.

117
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:25,968
‪Yeah, I love stuff like this.

118
00:06:26,552 --> 00:06:28,763
‪Is that water?
‪Wait, are we drinking tap water?

119
00:06:28,846 --> 00:06:31,474
‪Hold on, let me open it. I'm curious.

120
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:35,520
‪-You see the letters here?
‪-Yeah, it's another puzzle.

121
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:36,771
‪They're letters.

122
00:06:37,855 --> 00:06:38,940
‪Letters.

123
00:06:41,192 --> 00:06:43,236
‪What do you think
‪about this Hanja-like character?

124
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:46,280
‪It looks like the character for 100,
‪but it's probably not Hanja, right?

125
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:47,573
‪-Don't think so.
‪-Just a hieroglyph?

126
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,117
‪Should we see if this can be opened?

127
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,868
‪-Open it, of course.
‪-Right?

128
00:06:50,952 --> 00:06:52,787
‪-There's a handle.
‪-Oh gosh! Oh, it's food.

129
00:06:54,163 --> 00:06:55,873
‪-I get scared easily.
‪-Baguettes? Darn it.

130
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:58,751
‪-I'm happy with baguettes. They're carbs.
‪-Sure. It could be worse.

131
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:00,795
‪About these two.

132
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,297
‪This is "food," and that's "water."

133
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,675
‪But look.

134
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,427
‪This means "to consume,"
‪and this means "water."

135
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:09,637
‪"Water that can be consumed."

136
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,889
‪-Really?
‪-The sign there shared the first letter.

137
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,934
‪-You're so smart. You're a genius.
‪-"Food that can be consumed."

138
00:07:15,017 --> 00:07:15,852
‪I think you're right.

139
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:18,146
‪There were two characters near the tap.

140
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:21,607
<i>‪One for "to consume," and one for "water."</i>

141
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:24,152
<i>‪And there was the character</i>
<i>‪for </i><i>‪"to </i><i>‪consume" </i><i>‪where the bread was.</i>

142
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:27,405
‪So we figured the hieroglyph that looks
‪like the Hanja character for 100

143
00:07:27,488 --> 00:07:29,740
‪must be related to things
‪that are consumed.

144
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:32,452
‪There are hourglasses here,
‪which is a bit unsettling.

145
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:33,744
‪Right.

146
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:37,248
‪Three hourglasses of all different sizes.

147
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:40,251
‪But why are these two characters repeated?

148
00:07:40,334 --> 00:07:42,753
‪I think each one represents a time.

149
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:44,714
‪Something like 10 minutes, 15 minutes,

150
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:46,674
‪-and 20 minutes.
‪-Right, that must be it.

151
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:47,633
‪-Yeah.
‪-You're right.

152
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,135
‪See the sun there?

153
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:50,178
‪It looks like an eye.

154
00:07:50,261 --> 00:07:52,555
‪The sun can stand in for time
‪if you think about it.

155
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:54,390
‪It could be connected.

156
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:57,602
‪That sun might change
‪from red to black later.

157
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:58,644
‪I think that's right.

158
00:07:58,728 --> 00:08:02,023
‪And what are these? They're mattresses.

159
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:03,107
‪For sleeping.

160
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:05,485
‪-Mattresses.
‪-Matrix?

161
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:07,069
‪There are mattresses underneath.

162
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:08,863
‪-With pillows.
‪-You're right.

163
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:11,199
‪So we're sleeping here?

164
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:12,700
‪I think so.

165
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:14,744
‪And I'm thinking a maximum of four people
‪can be here.

166
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:16,829
‪There are four mattresses and four colors.

167
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,206
‪Only four can be in the exile zone.

168
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:20,291
‪Four people max, huh?

169
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,294
‪There seemed to be four spots total,

170
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:25,546
‪so I wondered if we had to wait
‪until all four arrived.

171
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:28,758
‪We thought the full capacity
‪was probably four.

172
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:31,135
‪I'm gonna go wash my face real quick.

173
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:33,137
‪-Why don't we change while we're at it?
‪-Sure.

174
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:37,767
‪I think we'll be staying here,
‪so let's get changed.

175
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:54,200
‪What's going on here?

176
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,786
‪Bound in coils of snakes?

177
00:08:57,995 --> 00:08:59,247
‪Why snakes?

178
00:09:00,998 --> 00:09:01,874
‪A path.

179
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:04,502
‪A person.

180
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:06,254
‪Stars.

181
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:10,174
‪Observation.

182
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:14,136
‪The birds ate this person
‪after attacking them.

183
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:16,722
‪The person in the center is being watched

184
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,599
‪from both sides.

185
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:22,353
‪Did you figure out anything?

186
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:24,480
‪Some common threads, here and there.

187
00:09:25,439 --> 00:09:27,733
‪I noticed this one thing.

188
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:28,818
‪-It's nothing major.
‪-Okay.

189
00:09:28,901 --> 00:09:30,987
‪I think the characters with the triangle
‪mean "a person."

190
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,071
‪The one up there? This one?

191
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:33,864
‪-I think that means "a person."
‪-Really?

192
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,741
‪And I think this means "to attack."

193
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:38,869
‪There are dots, diacritics, and bars.

194
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:39,996
‪Oh, so they're all different.

195
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:42,081
‪The angles must be different
‪for a reason.

196
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,584
‪You begin to see a pattern
‪if you look long enough.

197
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:46,877
‪They're basically
‪like Egyptian hieroglyphs.

198
00:09:48,546 --> 00:09:51,757
‪We're gonna have to
‪go through them one by one.

199
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:04,061
‪"The snake consumes birds."

200
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:05,730
‪That's it.

201
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:06,731
‪"The birds…"

202
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:08,316
‪What do they eat?

203
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:09,400
‪Worms?

204
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:12,278
‪"The birds consume the worm."

205
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:14,822
‪Can these two be the verb

206
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,157
‪and these the objects?

207
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:19,201
‪Yeah, that's definitely the verb.

208
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:21,203
‪I looked through, and as you said,

209
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:23,080
‪-the top parts are different.
‪-Yeah.

210
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:24,665
‪Dots, bars, and diacritics.

211
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:26,250
‪I found what makes them different.

212
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:27,335
‪It's this.

213
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:31,631
‪"The person." This is a noun.

214
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:33,007
‪"To consume." This is a verb.

215
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:34,300
‪-The dot means verb?
‪-Yeah.

216
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:35,926
‪-You see the one with a line over it?
‪-Yeah?

217
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:37,803
‪That's an object and a noun.

218
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:39,555
‪So the bar works like that.

219
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:42,475
‪-So the bar--
‪-So, "The person consumes the fruit."

220
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:44,477
‪-"Fruit"?
‪-This person's picking one.

221
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,937
‪-You're right.
‪-Looks like an apple.

222
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:49,065
‪So the syntax is like that of English.

223
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:51,233
‪And "drinking water" has a diacritic,

224
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:52,860
‪making it "water that can be consumed."

225
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:55,237
‪-Water is a noun.
‪-Right.

226
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,322
