<i>‪Yi Do, or Stella would do.</i>

1143
00:50:13,969 --> 00:50:15,262
<i>‪So I thought I'd give it my all.</i>

1144
00:50:16,304 --> 00:50:19,850
<i>‪I'm terrible at things</i>
<i>‪like </i><i>‪puzzles </i><i>‪or </i><i>‪Rubik's </i><i>‪Cube.</i>

1145
00:50:20,517 --> 00:50:22,978
‪But youth and stamina are on my side,

1146
00:50:23,603 --> 00:50:25,647
‪so I'll give it everything I've got.

1147
00:50:25,731 --> 00:50:28,483
<i>‪I love stuff like this.</i>

1148
00:50:28,984 --> 00:50:33,029
‪It's been a while, so I'm happy
‪that I have a new puzzle to solve.

1149
00:50:39,119 --> 00:50:40,537
‪This works.

1150
00:50:52,090 --> 00:50:53,258
‪That's not gonna work.

1151
00:50:55,719 --> 00:50:59,431
<i>‪Every time I tried to fit one Piece in,</i>
<i>‪I had to take another out.</i>

1152
00:51:06,396 --> 00:51:08,565
<i>‪Everything just collapsed</i>
<i>‪when I pulled one out,</i>

1153
00:51:08,648 --> 00:51:11,359
‪so I had to go back to square one,
‪over and over again.

1154
00:51:15,822 --> 00:51:18,366
<i>‪Going at it randomly just didn't work.</i>

1155
00:51:18,450 --> 00:51:20,744
<i>‪I thought I'd try sorting them out</i>
<i>‪by matching shapes.</i>

1156
00:51:22,746 --> 00:51:25,707
<i>‪There were two pairs of matching Pieces,</i>

1157
00:51:25,791 --> 00:51:27,709
<i>‪so I separated them</i>
<i>‪from the ones that didn't.</i>

1158
00:51:27,793 --> 00:51:31,213
<i>‪I tried arranging everything in order,</i>
<i>‪and I put the matching ones at the end</i>

1159
00:51:31,296 --> 00:51:33,089
<i>‪and tried to work from there,</i>

1160
00:51:33,173 --> 00:51:34,800
<i>‪but it didn't work at all.</i>

1161
00:51:35,634 --> 00:51:39,387
<i>‪The slots were all over the place</i>
<i>‪with no rhyme or reason.</i>

1162
00:51:39,471 --> 00:51:40,514
<i>‪I was just lost.</i>

1163
00:51:40,597 --> 00:51:45,811
‪I kept stacking from the top down,
‪but none of the combinations worked.

1164
00:51:45,894 --> 00:51:48,230
<i>‪So I kept trying to </i><i>‪think </i><i>‪of</i>
<i>‪all the different combos.</i>

1165
00:51:49,356 --> 00:51:50,273
‪Damn.

1166
00:51:54,152 --> 00:51:57,531
<i>‪The Pieces distributed in </i>‪The Devil's Plan
<i>‪are all of the same type,</i>

1167
00:51:57,614 --> 00:52:00,033
<i>‪and twelve of them are assembled into one.</i>

1168
00:52:00,116 --> 00:52:04,162
<i>‪But in Piece Puzzle, </i><i>‪eight </i><i>‪Pieces</i>
<i>‪of five different types are used.</i>

1169
00:52:04,246 --> 00:52:08,542
<i>‪The Pieces are similar</i>
<i>‪but subtly different, </i><i>‪making </i><i>‪this </i><i>‪harder,</i>

1170
00:52:08,625 --> 00:52:10,794
<i>‪and patience and focus will be required.</i>

1171
00:52:39,865 --> 00:52:42,284
<i>‪Nucksal, you have survived.</i>

1172
00:52:43,118 --> 00:52:44,953
<i>‪Please remain at your spot.</i>

1173
00:52:45,036 --> 00:52:46,246
‪I'm jealous.

1174
00:52:46,329 --> 00:52:47,706
‪So it's possible, huh?

1175
00:52:47,789 --> 00:52:49,040
‪I'm completely lost.

1176
00:52:49,541 --> 00:52:53,503
<i>‪It was structured</i>
<i>‪like </i><i>‪building </i><i>‪a highly complex lock.</i>

1177
00:52:53,587 --> 00:52:54,504
<i>‪So looking at it,</i>

1178
00:52:54,588 --> 00:52:58,508
<i>‪I realized the gaps are different</i>
<i>‪because everything has to fit together,</i>

1179
00:52:58,592 --> 00:53:00,969
<i>‪forming one giant lock shape,</i>

1180
00:53:01,052 --> 00:53:03,138
‪and the last Piece
‪gets slotted in to complete it.

1181
00:53:03,221 --> 00:53:04,639
<i>‪So I kept holding up two Pieces at a time</i>

1182
00:53:04,723 --> 00:53:07,976
<i>‪to find a gap big enough</i>
<i>‪to slide one Piece in.</i>

1183
00:53:14,649 --> 00:53:17,402
<i>‪When I found the right fit,</i>
<i>‪it fell into place.</i>

1184
00:53:19,154 --> 00:53:21,865
‪At least I came in first on this one.

1185
00:53:21,948 --> 00:53:23,116
‪It feels good.

1186
00:53:23,700 --> 00:53:24,701
‪Done.

1187
00:53:28,455 --> 00:53:29,956
‪The four sides…

1188
00:53:31,333 --> 00:53:32,751
‪How is this even possible?

1189
00:53:33,668 --> 00:53:36,588
<i>‪Seeing someone else finish</i>
<i>‪made the gap feel enormous.</i>

1190
00:53:37,172 --> 00:53:41,343
‪I really thought I couldn't figure it out,
‪but I kept pushing myself not to give up.

1191
00:53:42,385 --> 00:53:43,303
<i>‪I still had no luck.</i>

1192
00:53:43,386 --> 00:53:45,889
<i>‪I suddenly felt this overwhelming urgency.</i>

1193
00:53:46,806 --> 00:53:48,141
‪Damn it.

1194
00:53:54,439 --> 00:53:55,941
‪This is way too hard.

1195
00:53:57,567 --> 00:53:59,569
‪Don't give up. Keep going, everyone.

1196
00:53:59,653 --> 00:54:00,570
‪You got this.

1197
00:54:01,071 --> 00:54:02,405
‪This is possible, right?

1198
00:54:02,489 --> 00:54:03,365
‪It is.

1199
00:54:05,200 --> 00:54:06,409
‪It is.

1200
00:54:06,493 --> 00:54:07,535
‪Even I did it.

1201
00:54:09,412 --> 00:54:15,043
<i>‪I learned that what mattered</i>
<i>‪was how deep the grooves were.</i>

1202
00:54:15,126 --> 00:54:18,046
<i>‪The open sides</i>
<i>‪came </i><i>‪in </i><i>‪either one and three,</i>

1203
00:54:18,129 --> 00:54:19,047
<i>‪or two and two.</i>

1204
00:54:19,130 --> 00:54:21,299
<i>‪Those were the only two options.</i>

1205
00:54:21,383 --> 00:54:24,010
‪So if the pattern came out
‪as open, closed, closed, open,

1206
00:54:24,094 --> 00:54:25,553
‪nothing could slot in.

1207
00:54:25,637 --> 00:54:29,182
<i>‪That's what I needed to watch out for</i>
<i>‪as I tried the different arrangements.</i>

1208
00:54:58,545 --> 00:54:59,838
<i>‪Stella Jang,</i>

1209
00:54:59,921 --> 00:55:01,339
<i>‪you have survived.</i>

1210
00:55:04,009 --> 00:55:05,552
<i>‪After I solved it,</i>

1211
00:55:05,635 --> 00:55:08,430
<i>‪I felt the satisfaction</i>
<i>‪of a job well done.</i>

1212
00:55:08,513 --> 00:55:12,267
‪And the completed form
‪was really beautiful.

1213
00:55:12,350 --> 00:55:15,437
<i>‪It was symmetrical</i>
<i>‪around </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪center </i><i>‪point.</i>

1214
00:55:21,818 --> 00:55:23,028
<i>‪There was only one spot left.</i>

1215
00:55:23,111 --> 00:55:25,572
<i>‪That's when my hands started sweating.</i>

1216
00:55:25,655 --> 00:55:27,991
<i>‪I think the setting</i>
<i>‪of </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪exile </i><i>‪zone </i><i>‪itself</i>

1217
00:55:28,616 --> 00:55:30,285
<i>‪amped up the pressure.</i>

1218
00:55:30,368 --> 00:55:32,162
‪Please don't give up.

1219
00:55:33,371 --> 00:55:35,665
<i>‪Honestly, it wasn't </i><i>‪about</i>
<i>‪who the competition was.</i>

1220
00:55:35,749 --> 00:55:39,919
<i>‪It was about how well</i>
<i>‪I understood the puzzle.</i>

1221
00:55:44,424 --> 00:55:47,218
<i>‪I gave everything I had</i>
<i>‪to figuring it out.</i>

1222
00:56:03,401 --> 00:56:05,487
<i>‪I was almost done.</i>

1223
00:56:05,570 --> 00:56:06,946
<i>‪I just needed to fit in two more.</i>

1224
00:56:07,489 --> 00:56:10,992
<i>‪I had to lift some</i>
<i>‪to </i><i>‪slot </i><i>‪them </i><i>‪in </i><i>‪between,</i>

1225
00:56:11,076 --> 00:56:13,995
<i>‪but it was just such a tight fit.</i>

1226
00:56:14,079 --> 00:56:15,955
<i>‪It was so tight that it got stuck.</i>

1227
00:56:16,039 --> 00:56:19,250
‪That's when I started getting frustrated.

1228
00:56:19,334 --> 00:56:20,251
<i>‪It was just too much.</i>

1229
00:56:51,241 --> 00:56:53,785
<i>‪That concludes the exile zone match.</i>

1230
00:56:55,245 --> 00:56:57,288
<i>‪Farewell, Yi Do.</i>

1231
00:56:58,665 --> 00:57:00,083
‪What the? I'm going down!

1232
00:57:00,166 --> 00:57:02,043
‪Just like that?

1233
00:57:03,128 --> 00:57:04,295
‪You did great.

1234
00:57:07,423 --> 00:57:08,466
‪This is scary.

1235
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:10,176
‪Good job, Yi Do.

1236
00:57:10,260 --> 00:57:14,806
<i>‪Jin-ho, Nucksal, and Stella</i>
<i>‪were all so good to me.</i>

1237
00:57:14,889 --> 00:57:19,561
<i>‪In the end, we worked together</i>
<i>‪to decode the hieroglyphics and symbols.</i>

1238
00:57:19,644 --> 00:57:23,273
<i>‪That was such a heartwarming experience.</i>

1239
00:57:23,356 --> 00:57:24,524
<i>‪I'm thankful.</i>

1240
00:57:24,607 --> 00:57:27,902
‪They still have the chance
‪to return to <i>‪The Devil's Plan,</i>

1241
00:57:27,986 --> 00:57:30,238
‪so I'm rooting for all of them.

1242
00:57:31,239 --> 00:57:32,198
‪Poor Yi Do.

1243
00:57:32,949 --> 00:57:35,493
‪She just got sucked in
‪without even getting to say goodbye.

1244
00:57:35,577 --> 00:57:38,246
‪Isn't this basically
‪the <i>‪Show Me the Money</i>‪ fire pit?

1245
00:57:38,329 --> 00:57:40,331
‪-Didn't even get to say a proper goodbye.
‪-I feel bad.

1246
00:57:40,415 --> 00:57:42,792
‪She worked really hard on that.

1247
00:57:42,876 --> 00:57:44,419
‪I'm hungry.

1248
00:57:44,502 --> 00:57:45,545
‪Eat some bread.

1249
00:57:46,671 --> 00:57:48,756
‪-That's all we got.
‪-Damn it.

1250
00:57:48,840 --> 00:57:50,633
‪I'm getting so sick of this.

1251
00:57:58,308 --> 00:57:59,184
‪By the way,

1252
00:57:59,267 --> 00:58:00,477
‪this is "clock."

1253
00:58:01,436 --> 00:58:02,520
‪"Clock"?

1254
00:58:03,104 --> 00:58:04,189
‪So here's the thing.

1255
00:58:06,065 --> 00:58:07,150
‪"Second," "minute," "hour."

1256
00:58:09,527 --> 00:58:13,114
‪"The number of seconds on a clock
‪is the sum of something."

1257
00:58:13,740 --> 00:58:15,533
‪"The number of minutes
‪is the sum of something."

1258
00:58:15,617 --> 00:58:17,368
‪"The number of hours
‪is the sum of something."

1259
00:58:17,452 --> 00:58:19,329
‪But that's also still speculation.

1260
00:58:19,412 --> 00:58:20,705
‪What could the spiral mean?

1261
00:58:20,788 --> 00:58:23,208
‪What could the spiral be?

1262
00:58:23,291 --> 00:58:25,251
‪That's the key.

1263
00:58:25,877 --> 00:58:27,712
‪It appears here too.

1264
00:58:28,338 --> 00:58:29,297
‪What's this?

1265
00:58:30,882 --> 00:58:32,509
‪"Bird creates…"

1266
00:58:32,592 --> 00:58:33,760
‪-"Egg."
‪-"Egg."

1267
00:58:33,843 --> 00:58:35,845
‪Maybe it's "next" or "follows"?

1268
00:58:36,554 --> 00:58:38,348
‪Some sort of conclusive statement.

1269
00:58:38,431 --> 00:58:40,725
‪Like when you're talking about
‪cause and effect.

1270
00:58:40,808 --> 00:58:42,894
‪BIRD, CREATE, EGG, CONCLUSION?

1271
00:58:42,977 --> 00:58:44,270
‪"Therefore"?

1272
00:58:44,354 --> 00:58:45,271
‪"And"?

1273
00:58:46,648 --> 00:58:47,899
‪"And so"?

1274
00:58:49,776 --> 00:58:50,860
‪What could this be?

1275
00:58:53,154 --> 00:58:54,322
‪Plural.

1276
00:58:54,405 --> 00:58:55,740
‪It's the plural marker.

1277
00:58:56,533 --> 00:58:57,784
‪"Bird creates eggs."

1278
00:58:58,701 --> 00:59:01,496
‪And that's "Small people
‪kill a large person."

1279
00:59:01,579 --> 00:59:02,413
‪No way.

1280
00:59:03,164 --> 00:59:04,874
‪-Stella, you're on a different level.
‪-Eureka!

1281
00:59:04,958 --> 00:59:06,376
‪It's the plural marker.

1282
00:59:07,293 --> 00:59:09,671
‪"Time sees something plural."

1283
00:59:11,756 --> 00:59:14,634
‪So much more will open up
‪once we figure out that U.

1284
00:59:15,385 --> 00:59:19,347
‪May I propose a theory?

1285
00:59:20,431 --> 00:59:21,933
‪I think

1286
00:59:22,016 --> 00:59:24,769
‪the U could mean "you."

1287
00:59:24,852 --> 00:59:25,687
‪The plural form?

1288
00:59:26,187 --> 00:59:28,106
‪That would make a lot of sense.

1289
00:59:28,189 --> 00:59:29,482
‪U means "you"?

1290
00:59:30,233 --> 00:59:31,776
‪Then this would be…

1291
00:59:31,859 --> 00:59:34,654
‪"Time sees you

1292
00:59:34,737 --> 00:59:36,489
‪above the sun"?

1293
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:37,407
‪Or "from above?"

1294
00:59:38,241 --> 00:59:40,660
‪So, "The black moon

1295
00:59:41,286 --> 00:59:42,120
‪exists."

1296
00:59:44,330 --> 00:59:45,790
‪-"Below."
‪-"Below"?

1297
00:59:46,708 --> 00:59:48,668
‪-Hold on.
‪-Are we sure "black moon" is right?

1298
00:59:48,751 --> 00:59:51,254
‪Isn't it more like
‪"It exists in a downward direction"?

1299
00:59:51,337 --> 00:59:52,171
‪"Downward direction"?

1300
00:59:52,255 --> 00:59:54,090
‪"Black," "below."

1301
00:59:54,173 --> 00:59:56,342
‪But the key point here is this.

1302
00:59:56,968 --> 00:59:58,094
‪Bird?

1303
00:59:58,177 --> 00:59:59,345
‪We know this one for certain.

1304
01:00:00,263 --> 01:00:02,765
‪"When the bird calls out six times…"

1305
01:00:02,849 --> 01:00:04,726
‪You see the one at the end
‪with the dot in the middle?

1306
01:00:04,809 --> 01:00:06,894
‪We think that's "shadow," right?

1307
01:00:08,104 --> 01:00:09,147
‪And "sun" is next to it.

1308
01:00:09,230 --> 01:00:11,149
‪So the sun rises, and a shadow appears.

1309
01:00:11,232 --> 01:00:15,403
‪"The sun creates your shadow."
‪That checks out.

1310
01:00:15,987 --> 01:00:19,365
‪I still think there should be something
‪that blocks the sun.

1311
01:00:20,491 --> 01:00:21,367
‪What could it be?

1312
01:00:22,493 --> 01:00:24,704
‪We're so close,

1313
01:00:24,787 --> 01:00:25,913
‪but it's missing one piece.

1314
01:00:25,997 --> 01:00:27,665
‪-We're missing the core chunk.
‪-Yeah, exactly.

1315
01:00:27,749 --> 01:00:31,878
‪I feel like
‪we should've solved one by now.

1316
01:00:31,961 --> 01:00:33,421
‪Then solve that one.

1317
01:00:35,048 --> 01:00:36,299
‪That one's the last resort.

1318
01:00:37,592 --> 01:00:39,135
‪I can't bring myself to flip them.

1319
01:00:39,218 --> 01:00:41,763
‪I feel bad for saying this,
‪but someone new will be here soon.

1320
01:00:42,472 --> 01:00:43,931
‪They can flip everything over.

1321
01:00:45,892 --> 01:00:46,934
‪I just can't bring myself to.

1322
01:00:48,519 --> 01:00:50,104
‪I wonder who's coming next.

1323
01:00:50,730 --> 01:00:52,190
‪I can't even remember who's left.

1324
01:00:52,273 --> 01:00:53,816
‪Whoever it is, hurry up.

1325
01:00:55,109 --> 01:00:57,820
<i>‪Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1326
01:00:58,446 --> 01:00:59,364
‪What happened to Shindong?

1327
01:00:59,447 --> 01:01:00,323
‪12TH PLACE: SHINDONG

1328
01:01:00,907 --> 01:01:01,741
‪What the?

1329
01:01:02,700 --> 01:01:03,576
‪What happened?

1330
01:01:04,952 --> 01:01:05,870
‪Bye.

1331
01:01:06,704 --> 01:01:08,164
‪-Goodbye.
‪-Great work.

1332
01:01:11,542 --> 01:01:12,502
‪What's this?

1333
01:01:13,127 --> 01:01:14,545
<i>‪When I opened the door,</i>

1334
01:01:14,629 --> 01:01:16,798
‪a red door and a blue door
‪were waiting for me.

1335
01:01:16,881 --> 01:01:18,466
‪They gave me a second chance.

1336
01:01:18,549 --> 01:01:19,842
‪I have to take it.

1337
01:01:19,926 --> 01:01:20,927
‪And I did.

1338
01:01:22,387 --> 01:01:23,304
‪I'll go.

1339
01:01:26,933 --> 01:01:28,267
‪Jeez, that scared me.

1340
01:01:33,481 --> 01:01:34,649
‪Someone's here.

1341
01:01:36,484 --> 01:01:37,610
‪Hello.

1342
01:01:40,196 --> 01:01:41,322
‪You're here already.

1343
01:01:41,406 --> 01:01:42,407
‪Hey, Shindong.

1344
01:01:43,241 --> 01:01:45,660
<i>‪Welcome to the exile zone.</i>

1345
01:01:46,285 --> 01:01:47,328
‪What is all this?

1346
01:01:50,373 --> 01:01:51,916
‪-You doing okay?
‪-Of course.

1347
01:01:51,999 --> 01:01:53,334
‪Someone's missing.

1348
01:01:53,418 --> 01:01:54,585
‪-She left.
‪-She did.

1349
01:01:54,669 --> 01:01:56,003
‪Yi Do left us.

1350
01:01:56,087 --> 01:01:57,380
‪-She just left?
‪-After a game.

1351
01:01:57,964 --> 01:02:00,049
‪Quite a fancy outfit you got there.

1352
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:02,802
‪This is what they handed out
‪in the living area.

1353
01:02:02,885 --> 01:02:04,971
‪You were in the living area.
‪How'd you end up here?

1354
01:02:05,054 --> 01:02:06,222
‪You won't believe it.

1355
01:02:06,931 --> 01:02:07,849
‪I got betrayed.

1356
01:02:07,932 --> 01:02:09,308
‪-You did?
‪-Won-young betrayed me.

1357
01:02:10,309 --> 01:02:11,811
‪I cried during my interview.

1358
01:02:12,520 --> 01:02:16,774
‪I was so confused
‪when I saw the red and blue doors.

1359
01:02:16,858 --> 01:02:19,026
‪Another drama in just two days.

1360
01:02:19,610 --> 01:02:21,320
‪So you were here for a day?

1361
01:02:21,404 --> 01:02:22,822
‪Do you happen to know what time it is?

1362
01:02:22,905 --> 01:02:24,449
‪I didn't check before coming.

1363
01:02:24,532 --> 01:02:26,409
‪It's been so long
‪since we last saw the time.

1364
01:02:26,492 --> 01:02:27,952
‪-Really?
‪-We have no sense of time.

1365
01:02:28,035 --> 01:02:29,871
‪Then how do you know
‪when to sleep and wake up?

1366
01:02:29,954 --> 01:02:31,247
‪-That changes.
‪-The light goes out.

1367
01:02:32,165 --> 01:02:33,624
‪We also get a bird call.

1368
01:02:33,708 --> 01:02:34,667
‪Really?

1369
01:02:34,751 --> 01:02:36,502
‪What is this place? Can I look around?

1370
01:02:37,295 --> 01:02:39,088
<i>‪When Shindong came, I was like "Oh man."</i>

1371
01:02:39,172 --> 01:02:42,258
‪But then I realized
‪he's a veteran of <i>‪Great Escape.</i>

1372
01:02:42,341 --> 01:02:43,301
‪I have high hopes.

1373
01:02:43,885 --> 01:02:47,430
<i>‪The first thing I did </i><i>‪was </i><i>‪look </i><i>‪around</i>
<i>‪for what I could do.</i>

1374
01:02:51,267 --> 01:02:53,478
‪-You've probably tried everything.
‪-That's where you came in.

1375
01:02:53,561 --> 01:02:54,395
‪No, not that.

1376
01:02:54,479 --> 01:02:56,647
‪Maybe the handle comes off,
‪and there's a magnet.

1377
01:02:57,398 --> 01:02:59,609
‪-You must've tried.
‪-A true escape room veteran.

1378
01:03:00,193 --> 01:03:01,402
‪We didn't try any of that.

1379
01:03:02,612 --> 01:03:03,613
‪Wait, what's this?

1380
01:03:05,323 --> 01:03:06,449
‪That's my T-shirt.

1381
01:03:06,532 --> 01:03:08,284
‪-Oh, sorry.
‪-It's fine.

1382
01:03:09,952 --> 01:03:12,538
‪This looks interesting. What is it?

1383
01:03:12,622 --> 01:03:15,458
‪When two dots are attached,
‪it means it's a color.

1384
01:03:15,541 --> 01:03:17,502
‪Yi Do told us that before she left.

1385
01:03:18,586 --> 01:03:20,463
‪-That's "salt color," and that's "white."
‪-"Salt color."

1386
01:03:22,256 --> 01:03:25,676
‪I wanna solve this one thing
‪if it's the last thing I do before I go.

1387
01:03:26,719 --> 01:03:29,180
‪It stands out so much like a tutorial.

1388
01:03:29,263 --> 01:03:30,097
‪You're right.

1389
01:03:30,681 --> 01:03:32,308
‪-How strange.
‪-Right?

1390
01:03:35,061 --> 01:03:36,521
‪I don't think it's anything.

1391
01:03:36,604 --> 01:03:38,189
‪It's probably just paint.

1392
01:03:43,986 --> 01:03:44,946
‪Nothing's happening.

1393
01:03:50,326 --> 01:03:51,202
‪What the?

1394
01:03:51,285 --> 01:03:52,119
‪It's going up.

1395
01:03:55,164 --> 01:03:55,998
‪It's coming out.

1396
01:03:56,082 --> 01:03:57,083
‪No way.

1397
01:03:57,166 --> 01:03:58,292
‪It's coming out.

1398
01:03:58,376 --> 01:03:59,210
‪Really?

1399
01:04:01,254 --> 01:04:02,088
‪Amazing.

1400
01:04:02,880 --> 01:04:03,714
‪What is it?

1401
01:04:03,798 --> 01:04:04,757
‪What is it?

1402
01:04:04,841 --> 01:04:06,092
‪It's a moon.

1403
01:04:06,175 --> 01:04:07,426
‪-Really?
‪-You're kidding.

1404
01:04:08,344 --> 01:04:09,846
‪We just had to turn it to open it?

1405
01:04:10,763 --> 01:04:13,057
‪-You just opened it yourself? For real?
‪-Yeah.

1406
01:04:13,599 --> 01:04:15,059
‪-That's amazing.
‪-Seriously.

1407
01:04:15,142 --> 01:04:16,769
‪-Way to go, <i>‪Great Escape.</i>
<i>‪-</i>‪That's right.

1408
01:04:16,853 --> 01:04:17,687
‪He's legit.

1409
01:04:17,770 --> 01:04:19,605
‪I can't believe this at all.

1410
01:04:19,689 --> 01:04:20,690
‪What's your deal?

1411
01:04:20,773 --> 01:04:22,817
‪It was incredible.

1412
01:04:22,900 --> 01:04:26,362
<i>‪Only Shindong would think to turn it.</i>

1413
01:04:26,445 --> 01:04:28,865
‪I honestly don't think
‪we would've figured that out

1414
01:04:28,948 --> 01:04:30,867
‪if it hadn't been for him.

1415
01:04:30,950 --> 01:04:33,369
‪Thank you, <i>‪Great Escape.</i>

1416
01:04:33,452 --> 01:04:35,288
‪Experience is everything.

1417
01:04:36,080 --> 01:04:38,165
‪Does this cover that spot over there?

1418
01:04:38,249 --> 01:04:39,667
‪Looks like it needs to go in there.

1419
01:04:40,167 --> 01:04:41,502
‪That would do it.

1420
01:04:41,586 --> 01:04:42,712
‪Are you sure?

1421
01:04:44,547 --> 01:04:46,299
‪Doesn't it look like it'd fit there?

1422
01:04:47,383 --> 01:04:49,427
‪It's pretty obvious
‪it's meant for that spot.

1423
01:04:49,510 --> 01:04:52,388
‪-It'd be perfect.
‪-I kept wondering how to cover that eye.

1424
01:04:52,471 --> 01:04:54,223
‪Okay, what do we do with this?

1425
01:04:54,307 --> 01:04:57,643
‪So if your prediction is right
‪and we interpreted this text correctly,

1426
01:04:59,270 --> 01:05:00,396
‪this means "black."

1427
01:05:00,479 --> 01:05:02,440
‪-It's "black hole."
‪-Okay.

1428
01:05:02,523 --> 01:05:04,692
‪-"Black hole"?
‪-Yeah.

1429
01:05:04,775 --> 01:05:07,153
‪Wait, this has to be "black moon."

1430
01:05:08,613 --> 01:05:09,697
‪-"Black moon."
‪-"Black moon."

1431
01:05:10,531 --> 01:05:12,158
‪"The black moon exists below."

1432
01:05:13,034 --> 01:05:14,160
‪No way.

1433
01:05:15,870 --> 01:05:20,082
‪I guess that was just a hint
‪about the location of the black moon.

1434
01:05:20,166 --> 01:05:21,042
‪"Black moon."

1435
01:05:21,125 --> 01:05:23,920
‪Yi Do got almost everything
‪right before she left.

1436
01:05:25,129 --> 01:05:27,632
‪-That's a real legacy.
‪-She left a legacy.

1437
01:05:27,715 --> 01:05:29,634
‪She's the one
‪who told us about the colors.

1438
01:05:29,717 --> 01:05:30,885
‪I know.

1439
01:05:30,968 --> 01:05:32,720
‪Can you decode that for me again?

1440
01:05:32,803 --> 01:05:34,347
‪I'll do it.

1441
01:05:34,430 --> 01:05:36,223
‪The latter half is still a bit unclear

1442
01:05:36,307 --> 01:05:39,852
‪because this character is used as a noun,
‪and we interpreted it as "shadow."

1443
01:05:40,853 --> 01:05:43,940
‪If this becomes a verb,
‪then is it "to cast a shadow"?

1444
01:05:44,941 --> 01:05:46,275
‪But this is "sun."

1445
01:05:46,984 --> 01:05:49,695
‪Then should this be,
‪"You cast a shadow over the sun"?

1446
01:05:51,155 --> 01:05:53,324
‪Shadow as a verb?

1447
01:05:53,407 --> 01:05:54,575
‪CAST A SHADOW

1448
01:05:54,659 --> 01:05:55,826
‪"Cover."

1449
01:05:55,910 --> 01:05:57,495
‪Yeah, that's it.

1450
01:05:57,578 --> 01:05:59,413
‪"When the bird calls out six times,

1451
01:06:00,039 --> 01:06:01,874
‪you cover the sun."

1452
01:06:03,709 --> 01:06:05,962
‪Maybe we can insert this
‪when the bird calls out.

1453
01:06:07,880 --> 01:06:09,423
‪You know what?

1454
01:06:10,257 --> 01:06:11,676
‪I think that comes down.

1455
01:06:12,718 --> 01:06:14,136
‪-It comes down?
‪-Yeah.

1456
01:06:14,220 --> 01:06:16,222
‪This morning,
‪the bird called out six times.

1457
01:06:16,806 --> 01:06:18,182
‪We found the moon now.

1458
01:06:19,058 --> 01:06:20,685
‪It'll come down
‪when the bird calls out next.

1459
01:06:20,768 --> 01:06:22,687
‪You hadn't found the moon yet,
‪so it didn't come down.

1460
01:06:22,770 --> 01:06:23,813
‪Yeah, I think so.

1461
01:06:23,896 --> 01:06:27,566
‪We should be able to insert this in there
‪if it comes down low enough.

1462
01:06:27,650 --> 01:06:29,986
‪I can't tell which one is "day"
‪and which one is "night."

1463
01:06:30,069 --> 01:06:32,780
‪But maybe it goes,
‪"When day ends and night comes,

1464
01:06:33,406 --> 01:06:36,283
‪you can see the path."

1465
01:06:36,367 --> 01:06:37,201
‪"The path."

1466
01:06:37,827 --> 01:06:39,078
‪And then,

1467
01:06:39,161 --> 01:06:40,579
‪"The black hole

1468
01:06:41,205 --> 01:06:43,416
‪exists in the middle of the path."

1469
01:06:44,625 --> 01:06:45,835
‪Then, this line must be saying

1470
01:06:45,918 --> 01:06:48,004
‪that a game starts
‪when the black hole appears.

1471
01:06:48,087 --> 01:06:49,547
‪-The second character means "game."
‪-"Game"?

1472
01:06:49,630 --> 01:06:51,465
‪"Time," "game," and "exists"?

1473
01:06:51,549 --> 01:06:52,967
‪Yeah.

1474
01:06:53,551 --> 01:06:56,178
‪That long text over there
‪has this as the title.

1475
01:06:56,262 --> 01:06:59,473
‪GAME OF TIME?

1476
01:06:59,557 --> 01:07:01,308
‪This is the reason the exile zone exists.

1477
01:07:01,392 --> 01:07:03,144
‪Then we need to figure out that game fast.

1478
01:07:04,186 --> 01:07:05,271
‪The numbers…

1479
01:07:08,274 --> 01:07:10,276
‪Can any of this be decoded at all?

1480
01:07:10,359 --> 01:07:11,902
‪-We've gotten quite far.
‪-None of it?

1481
01:07:11,986 --> 01:07:15,156
‪"The clock equals the numbers of time."

1482
01:07:17,324 --> 01:07:19,326
‪This is "The clock…"

1483
01:07:19,410 --> 01:07:21,203
‪Nucksal, what was this again?

1484
01:07:21,829 --> 01:07:23,831
‪No idea. Can't figure it out.

1485
01:07:23,914 --> 01:07:27,501
‪I don't even know where to start.
‪I can't decode the upper lines.

1486
01:07:27,585 --> 01:07:33,007
‪So far, we have "The sum of the numbers
‪on the clock in a horizontal row

1487
01:07:33,090 --> 01:07:36,761
‪equals the sum of the numbers
‪in a vertical row

1488
01:07:37,678 --> 01:07:40,806
‪equals the sum of the numbers
‪in a diagonal line."

1489
01:07:41,599 --> 01:07:43,392
‪But we're not sure about those.

1490
01:07:44,101 --> 01:07:48,189
‪I originally assumed they meant
‪the second, minute, and hour hands.

1491
01:07:50,149 --> 01:07:52,651
‪Did you guess this was "clock"
‪because it resembles that?

1492
01:07:52,735 --> 01:07:54,487
‪I mean, they're practically identical.

1493
01:07:55,279 --> 01:07:57,364
‪Are "horizontal," "vertical,"
‪and "diagonal" right?

1494
01:07:58,282 --> 01:08:00,534
‪-Probably not.
‪-It might not be.

1495
01:08:02,161 --> 01:08:04,830
‪Even now, so much remains hidden.

1496
01:08:05,498 --> 01:08:07,374
‪We just need to figure out this game.

1497
01:08:07,958 --> 01:08:10,127
‪This really feels like practice.

1498
01:08:10,211 --> 01:08:12,379
‪"Nucksal, you have one hour."

1499
01:08:12,463 --> 01:08:15,716
‪A one-hour problem makes me sick
‪just thinking about it.

1500
01:08:16,425 --> 01:08:18,511
‪"Nucksal, you have failed."

1501
01:08:18,594 --> 01:08:20,805
‪"Nucksal, please stand by the door."

1502
01:08:22,223 --> 01:08:24,225
‪"Please choose a door."

1503
01:08:24,308 --> 01:08:26,519
‪I'm leaving. Let me go.

1504
01:08:26,602 --> 01:08:28,270
‪Please let me go.

1505
01:08:28,354 --> 01:08:31,774
‪Is Yi Do out there somewhere,
‪happily solving puzzles

1506
01:08:31,857 --> 01:08:33,609
‪in a new place?

1507
01:08:34,193 --> 01:08:35,736
‪Somewhere even deeper than here.

1508
01:08:35,820 --> 01:08:37,655
‪"This place is below the exile zone."

1509
01:08:37,738 --> 01:08:38,739
‪The dung heap zone.

1510
01:08:38,823 --> 01:08:39,907
‪"The maggot mass zone."

1511
01:08:41,200 --> 01:08:44,203
‪How much deeper must we go?

1512
01:08:45,287 --> 01:08:47,665
‪Just let me die. I'll go.

1513
01:08:48,249 --> 01:08:51,794
‪"There are still 48,032 doors remaining."

1514
01:08:51,877 --> 01:08:53,546
‪That sounds horrifying.

1515
01:08:54,964 --> 01:08:57,633
‪I really wanna insert the stone tablet
‪into that eye before I go.

1516
01:09:00,469 --> 01:09:01,303
‪Here we go.

1517
01:09:01,887 --> 01:09:02,721
‪It's going down.

1518
01:09:04,723 --> 01:09:06,725
‪And once again,
‪one of us will be going home.

1519
01:09:07,393 --> 01:09:10,187
<i>‪We will now begin the exile zone match.</i>

1520
01:09:10,896 --> 01:09:13,858
<i>‪Please make your way</i>
<i>‪to a spot of your choice.</i>

1521
01:09:19,530 --> 01:09:23,075
<i>‪The two lowest-ranking players</i>
<i>‪in the exile zone match</i>

1522
01:09:23,868 --> 01:09:25,661
<i>‪will go home.</i>

1523
01:09:25,744 --> 01:09:26,829
‪Two people?

1524
01:09:28,622 --> 01:09:30,916
<i>‪It's not one but two eliminations.</i>

1525
01:09:31,000 --> 01:09:33,878
<i>‪This just got intense.</i>

1526
01:09:33,961 --> 01:09:36,130
‪Two? Damn it.

1527
01:09:36,213 --> 01:09:39,216
‪My odds of staying are 50-50 now.

1528
01:09:41,510 --> 01:09:43,095
<i>‪The second exile zone match is</i>

1529
01:09:43,846 --> 01:09:45,973
<i>‪Spot the Difference.</i>

1530
01:09:46,557 --> 01:09:49,059
‪Difference as in changed?

1531
01:09:49,143 --> 01:09:53,355
<i>‪Players will first view</i>
<i>‪the original image on the monitor.</i>

1532
01:09:54,607 --> 01:09:57,234
<i>‪The original image will disappear</i>
<i>‪after three minutes,</i>

1533
01:09:57,318 --> 01:10:00,905
<i>‪and ten seconds later,</i>
<i>‪the altered image will be revealed.</i>

1534
01:10:00,988 --> 01:10:03,824
<i>‪There are five differences in total.</i>

1535
01:10:03,908 --> 01:10:05,784
<i>‪Within the two-minute time limit,</i>

1536
01:10:05,868 --> 01:10:09,246
<i>‪players must find the differences</i>
<i>‪and mark them with an X.</i>

1537
01:10:09,914 --> 01:10:15,836
<i>‪The center of the X must be placed</i>
<i>‪precisely on the altered spot,</i>

1538
01:10:15,920 --> 01:10:19,298
<i>‪and only five marks can be made.</i>

1539
01:10:19,882 --> 01:10:23,844
<i>‪Each correct answer </i><i>‪is </i><i>‪worth </i><i>‪one </i><i>‪point,</i>

1540
01:10:23,928 --> 01:10:26,347
<i>‪and the game will run for three rounds.</i>

1541
01:10:26,430 --> 01:10:29,391
<i>‪The two players</i>
<i>‪with the fewest correct answers</i>

1542
01:10:29,475 --> 01:10:31,227
<i>‪will go home.</i>

1543
01:10:31,310 --> 01:10:34,521
<i>‪The game will now begin.</i>

1544
01:10:35,522 --> 01:10:36,732
‪I'm done for.

1545
01:10:38,025 --> 01:10:39,735
<i>‪This is my absolute weakness.</i>

1546
01:10:39,818 --> 01:10:42,696
‪The Devil's Plan
<i>‪really </i><i>‪does </i><i>‪come down to memory.</i>

1547
01:10:42,780 --> 01:10:46,116
<i>‪I'm really bad at looking at something</i>
<i>‪and memorizing it.</i>

1548
01:10:46,200 --> 01:10:48,994
<i>‪Regardless, I still hoped</i>
<i>‪I could pull it off.</i>

1549
01:10:49,078 --> 01:10:51,664
<i>‪Round 1 will now begin.</i>

1550
01:10:52,289 --> 01:10:53,791
<i>‪Here is the original image.</i>

1551
01:10:58,712 --> 01:11:00,965
‪Are you serious? It's too big.

1552
01:11:01,632 --> 01:11:03,968
‪They're fishing.

1553
01:11:04,635 --> 01:11:06,387
<i>‪I've picked up a few tricks along the way.</i>

1554
01:11:06,470 --> 01:11:09,056
‪I tried to memorize it like a story.

1555
01:11:09,640 --> 01:11:10,891
‪The bucket is filled with water.

1556
01:11:12,518 --> 01:11:14,144
‪He's wearing rubber boots.

1557
01:11:15,437 --> 01:11:17,189
‪Straw hat, picnic mat.

1558
01:11:18,816 --> 01:11:20,192
‪Foxtails.

1559
01:11:20,276 --> 01:11:21,402
‪Fish.

1560
01:11:21,485 --> 01:11:25,155
<i>‪The first thing I memorized</i>
<i>‪was the colors.</i>

1561
01:11:25,739 --> 01:11:27,741
<i>‪For </i><i>‪example, </i><i>‪red, </i><i>‪green, </i><i>‪blue, </i><i>‪blue, </i><i>‪blue.</i>

1562
01:11:27,825 --> 01:11:29,910
<i>‪I focused on the key colors.</i>

1563
01:11:30,411 --> 01:11:32,496
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1564
01:11:34,123 --> 01:11:36,333
<i>‪Here is the altered image.</i>

1565
01:11:40,296 --> 01:11:42,506
‪ANSWERS WILL BE REVEALED TO VIEWERS FIRST

1566
01:12:48,405 --> 01:12:50,282
<i>‪Ten seconds remaining.</i>

1567
01:12:58,248 --> 01:13:00,000
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1568
01:13:04,505 --> 01:13:07,424
<i>‪Here are the players' scores for Round 1.</i>

1569
01:13:14,681 --> 01:13:17,101
<i>‪Round 2 will now begin.</i>

1570
01:13:17,184 --> 01:13:19,019
<i>‪Here is the original image.</i>

1571
01:13:30,364 --> 01:13:31,740
<i>‪Compared to the first round,</i>

1572
01:13:31,824 --> 01:13:34,618
<i>‪there were a lot more characters.</i>

1573
01:13:34,701 --> 01:13:36,370
‪A woman with a bun

1574
01:13:37,579 --> 01:13:38,747
‪wearing a red shirt

1575
01:13:39,373 --> 01:13:41,125
‪is weighing spinach on a scale.

1576
01:13:44,128 --> 01:13:45,129
‪Zero grams.

1577
01:13:46,964 --> 01:13:50,134
‪There are apples. Apples here and there.

1578
01:13:51,593 --> 01:13:53,429
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1579
01:13:54,221 --> 01:13:56,515
<i>‪Here is the altered image.</i>

1580
01:14:46,565 --> 01:14:48,108
‪Dang, I don't know.

1581
01:15:02,080 --> 01:15:03,707
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1582
01:15:05,501 --> 01:15:08,420
<i>‪Here are the players' scores for Round 2.</i>

1583
01:15:14,092 --> 01:15:16,053
‪Damn it.

1584
01:15:16,136 --> 01:15:16,970
‪You're all so good.

1585
01:15:17,054 --> 01:15:19,097
<i>‪I realized everyone was locked in.</i>

1586
01:15:19,181 --> 01:15:20,140
<i>‪I knew I was in trouble.</i>

1587
01:15:20,849 --> 01:15:23,352
<i>‪I got four right, and I was still last.</i>

1588
01:15:23,435 --> 01:15:26,188
<i>‪I thought, "I'm done for.</i>
<i>‪How do I get out of this alive?"</i>

1589
01:15:26,772 --> 01:15:28,899
<i>‪Round 3 will now begin.</i>

1590
01:15:29,525 --> 01:15:31,276
<i>‪Here is the original image.</i>

1591
01:15:35,989 --> 01:15:36,907
‪It's so big.

1592
01:15:36,990 --> 01:15:38,075
<i>‪The image got bigger.</i>

1593
01:15:38,158 --> 01:15:40,786
<i>‪There were dolphins and sharks.</i>

1594
01:15:43,789 --> 01:15:47,668
‪A dolphin wearing a hat and a whistle

1595
01:15:47,751 --> 01:15:49,169
‪is acting as a referee.

1596
01:15:49,253 --> 01:15:51,296
‪Blue ice box, red ice box.

1597
01:15:51,380 --> 01:15:53,966
‪Phone, coffee, book.

1598
01:15:54,049 --> 01:15:57,553
‪They've gone off to play,
‪leaving behind a pink beach mat.

1599
01:15:59,638 --> 01:16:01,431
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1600
01:16:03,600 --> 01:16:05,435
<i>‪Here is the altered image.</i>

1601
01:16:31,503 --> 01:16:33,505
‪What was it again? The parasol?

1602
01:16:35,841 --> 01:16:37,718
‪Damn it, I don't think that's it.

1603
01:16:43,348 --> 01:16:44,725
‪Maybe this one?

1604
01:17:07,581 --> 01:17:09,249
<i>‪Ten seconds remaining.</i>

1605
01:17:24,598 --> 01:17:26,475
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1606
01:17:30,937 --> 01:17:32,064
‪That last one was so hard.

1607
01:17:32,648 --> 01:17:36,276
<i>‪Here are the players' scores for Round 3.</i>

1608
01:17:40,197 --> 01:17:41,281
‪Damn it.

1609
01:17:41,365 --> 01:17:43,784
<i>‪Nucksal has a total of nine points.</i>

1610
01:17:44,409 --> 01:17:46,411
<i>‪Stella Jang has a total of ten points.</i>

1611
01:17:47,162 --> 01:17:49,039
<i>‪Shindong has a total of nine points.</i>

1612
01:17:49,748 --> 01:17:52,167
<i>‪Hong Jin-ho has a total of eight points.</i>

1613
01:17:54,461 --> 01:17:57,297
<i>‪Farewell, Hong Jin-ho.</i>

1614
01:18:00,342 --> 01:18:01,301
‪Jin-ho!

1615
01:18:03,136 --> 01:18:04,471
‪-Good luck!
‪-Jin-ho.

1616
01:18:04,554 --> 01:18:06,223
‪-Goodbye.
‪-Good luck.

1617
01:18:07,974 --> 01:18:10,602
<i>‪I realized I'm not what I used to be.</i>

1618
01:18:11,144 --> 01:18:16,525
‪You could just see Nucksal and Stella
‪quickly accept the situation

1619
01:18:16,608 --> 01:18:19,486
<i>‪and push ahead with the burning drive</i>
<i>‪to give everything they've got.</i>

1620
01:18:19,569 --> 01:18:21,947
<i>‪They were always studying, always pushing.</i>

1621
01:18:22,531 --> 01:18:25,367
<i>‪I used to be like that too.</i>

1622
01:18:25,450 --> 01:18:30,622
‪I think those are the things
‪that'll stay with me for a long time.

1623
01:18:32,541 --> 01:18:35,001
<i>‪Nucksal and Shindong</i>

1624
01:18:35,085 --> 01:18:39,131
<i>‪will play a tiebreaker round</i>
<i>‪to determine who will be eliminated.</i>

1625
01:18:40,257 --> 01:18:41,258
‪Good luck!

1626
01:18:41,883 --> 01:18:45,679
<i>‪In the tiebreaker round,</i>
<i>‪the image will be shown for two minutes.</i>

1627
01:18:46,847 --> 01:18:48,473
<i>‪Here is the original image.</i>

1628
01:18:59,151 --> 01:19:01,862
<i>‪The image looked easy to memorize.</i>

1629
01:19:01,945 --> 01:19:05,407
‪I kept missing the colors
‪in the earlier rounds,

1630
01:19:05,490 --> 01:19:08,368
<i>‪so I focused on the colors of the pants</i>

1631
01:19:08,994 --> 01:19:10,162
<i>‪and the shoes.</i>

1632
01:19:10,245 --> 01:19:12,164
<i>‪I was sure they'd come up.</i>

1633
01:19:14,666 --> 01:19:17,335
<i>‪I scanned everyone in the café.</i>

1634
01:19:18,336 --> 01:19:22,007
<i>‪I memorized the positions and colors</i>
<i>‪of the cups on top of the coffee machine.</i>

1635
01:19:22,090 --> 01:19:24,050
<i>‪I also scanned the apartment buildings</i>
<i>‪in </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪background.</i>

1636
01:19:24,134 --> 01:19:26,636
<i>‪I thought it was pretty doable.</i>

1637
01:19:26,720 --> 01:19:30,432
<i>‪I felt like I could score as high as I did</i>
<i>‪in the first two rounds.</i>

1638
01:19:30,515 --> 01:19:32,809
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1639
01:19:33,393 --> 01:19:35,312
<i>‪Here is the altered image.</i>

1640
01:20:01,838 --> 01:20:03,924
<i>‪I remembered where things were,</i>

1641
01:20:04,007 --> 01:20:07,302
<i>‪but the colors</i>
<i>‪just wouldn't come to me this round.</i>

1642
01:20:22,859 --> 01:20:25,362
<i>‪I quickly marked all five,</i>
<i>‪one after another.</i>

1643
01:20:30,992 --> 01:20:32,702
<i>‪Ten seconds remaining.</i>

1644
01:20:42,420 --> 01:20:45,048
<i>‪The moment I heard</i>
<i>‪the </i><i>‪ten-second </i><i>‪heads-up,</i>

1645
01:20:45,757 --> 01:20:47,509
<i>‪I noticed what was outside the window.</i>

1646
01:20:50,929 --> 01:20:53,056
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

1647
01:20:54,599 --> 01:20:56,893
<i>‪Nucksal has scored three points.</i>

1648
01:20:56,977 --> 01:20:59,813
<i>‪Shindong has scored four points.</i>

1649
01:21:00,730 --> 01:21:03,650
<i>‪That concludes the exile zone match.</i>

1650
01:21:03,733 --> 01:21:05,986
<i>‪Farewell, Nucksal.</i>

1651
01:21:09,406 --> 01:21:10,574
‪Take care of the rest for me.

1652
01:21:11,992 --> 01:21:16,496
‪My goal wasn't even to make it back.

1653
01:21:16,580 --> 01:21:19,624
‪As we kept solving things,
‪the pieces started coming together.

1654
01:21:20,125 --> 01:21:26,548
<i>‪I thought something big might happen</i>
<i>‪if we inserted </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪black </i><i>‪moon </i><i>‪tomorrow.</i>

1655
01:21:27,132 --> 01:21:29,092
‪I'm most disappointed about missing that.

1656
01:21:29,175 --> 01:21:32,596
‪So even if I had to do it all over again,

1657
01:21:33,388 --> 01:21:35,181
<i>‪I'm sure I'd choose that door again.</i>

1658
01:21:37,225 --> 01:21:38,226
‪The door to the exile zone.

1659
01:21:42,522 --> 01:21:44,983
‪It feels empty with half of us gone.

1660
01:21:45,066 --> 01:21:48,028
‪Yeah, it wouldn't feel this empty
‪if it had been just one person.

1661
01:21:48,111 --> 01:21:50,655
‪But what's with
‪these heavy-handed eliminations?

1662
01:21:51,615 --> 01:21:57,412
‪Truth is, I'd already drifted pretty far
‪from the idea of winning this competition.

1663
01:21:57,913 --> 01:22:01,875
‪But watching Nucksal
‪and Jin-ho leave like that,

1664
01:22:02,459 --> 01:22:05,295
‪I realized I needed to do something
‪about my rotten mentality.

1665
01:22:06,504 --> 01:22:09,090
‪But I have to say, I'd feel less upset
‪if I were eliminated now.

1666
01:22:09,716 --> 01:22:12,636
‪We've come too far not to see it through.
‪This is gonna be something huge.

1667
01:22:12,719 --> 01:22:16,431
‪I wouldn't really mind if I'm sent home
‪as long as the others make it.

1668
01:22:16,514 --> 01:22:19,059
‪You'd better stop
‪all that rotten mentality nonsense.

1669
01:22:19,142 --> 01:22:22,395
‪I am rotten. I came here rotten.

1670
01:22:23,313 --> 01:22:24,272
‪I feel like that too,

1671
01:22:24,356 --> 01:22:26,942
‪but since we made it this far,
‪let's make it out of here alive.

1672
01:22:27,525 --> 01:22:29,277
‪Who knows? We all just might.

1673
01:22:31,279 --> 01:22:32,781
‪It doesn't matter anymore

1674
01:22:32,906 --> 01:22:35,283
‪whether I'm here,
‪in prison, or anywhere else.

1675
01:22:35,367 --> 01:22:36,993
‪I just need to survive one more day.

1676
01:22:37,911 --> 01:22:39,621
<i>‪The whole mindset of</i>
<i>‪"Oh, I'll be fine if I go home now"</i>

1677
01:22:39,704 --> 01:22:41,456
<i>‪and "I've been here two nights,</i>
<i>‪so </i><i>‪that's </i><i>‪enough"</i>

1678
01:22:41,539 --> 01:22:43,375
‪just has to go.

1679
01:22:44,459 --> 01:22:47,212
‪Regardless of who comes,

1680
01:22:47,295 --> 01:22:51,049
‪the four of us need to finish this fast
‪and try it tomorrow morning.

1681
01:22:51,132 --> 01:22:53,009
‪I hope someone good at puzzles
‪gets eliminated.

1682
01:22:53,093 --> 01:22:53,927
‪I know.

1683
01:22:57,847 --> 01:22:59,140
‪Is it me?

1684
01:23:02,185 --> 01:23:03,144
‪Damn.

1685
01:23:04,104 --> 01:23:05,313
‪So that's how things were.

1686
01:23:06,064 --> 01:23:07,399
‪Why is it so heavy?

1687
01:23:09,192 --> 01:23:11,444
‪Hold on, I recognize that voice.

1688
01:23:13,530 --> 01:23:14,364
‪Hi.

1689
01:23:14,447 --> 01:23:15,865
‪No way. You've been sleeping here?

1690
01:23:15,949 --> 01:23:18,702
‪I've been here for two nights already!

1691
01:23:18,785 --> 01:23:19,786
‪What is all this?

1692
01:23:21,079 --> 01:23:22,080
‪Welcome, everyone.

1693
01:23:22,163 --> 01:23:24,124
‪We're so happy to see you,

1694
01:23:24,207 --> 01:23:25,917
‪and we have so much to catch you up on.

1695
01:23:26,001 --> 01:23:28,461
‪-There's just so much information.
‪-What is this? A team game?

1696
01:23:29,754 --> 01:23:30,755
‪Who's that?

1697
01:23:30,839 --> 01:23:35,051
‪I saw this bum on the floor
‪and wondered who it was.

1698
01:23:35,135 --> 01:23:37,429
‪Where should I begin? Mr. Shindong.

1699
01:23:38,555 --> 01:23:42,183
‪Mr. Shindong, we have some new members.

1700
01:23:46,563 --> 01:23:47,731
‪-Seok-jin.
‪-Hello.

1701
01:23:47,814 --> 01:23:48,898
‪How'd you end up here?

1702
01:23:49,441 --> 01:23:50,775
‪I got shot.

1703
01:23:50,859 --> 01:23:52,819
‪-We played Russian Roulette.
‪-During roulette.

1704
01:23:52,902 --> 01:23:55,321
‪Wait, that means yesterday…

1705
01:23:55,947 --> 01:23:59,325
‪Let me just cover the relevant information

1706
01:23:59,409 --> 01:24:01,036
‪-Yes, please.
‪-as quickly as possible.

1707
01:24:01,119 --> 01:24:03,455
‪Basically, we're stuck
‪in this timeless place.

1708
01:24:03,538 --> 01:24:05,749
‪Nothing changes.
‪We're stuck in this same setup.

1709
01:24:05,832 --> 01:24:07,417
‪-What?
‪-Always.

1710
01:24:08,043 --> 01:24:11,046
‪The only way to tell time here
‪is when someone new arrives.

1711
01:24:12,297 --> 01:24:15,008
‪In other words, a slightly open prison.

1712
01:24:15,675 --> 01:24:18,303
‪What did I do in my past life
‪to end up in exile?

1713
01:24:18,386 --> 01:24:20,555
‪But even the great Jeong Yak-yong
‪was exiled.

1714
01:24:20,638 --> 01:24:23,183
‪I think I can turn this around
‪if I just keep my head straight.

1715
01:24:23,266 --> 01:24:26,436
‪When did you start working on this?

1716
01:24:26,519 --> 01:24:28,980
‪Yi Do and Nucksal

1717
01:24:29,064 --> 01:24:32,817
‪had already decoded
‪a lot of the hieroglyphs.

1718
01:24:32,901 --> 01:24:37,238
‪I have all the information obtained
‪by the people who were here before me.

1719
01:24:37,322 --> 01:24:39,824
‪-I'm the keeper of this place's history.
‪-You are.

1720
01:24:39,908 --> 01:24:41,242
‪We need to learn everything she knows.

1721
01:24:41,326 --> 01:24:43,495
‪-She's like a living cultural heritage.
‪-Totally.

1722
01:24:43,578 --> 01:24:46,956
‪This knowledge
‪gets passed down as a legacy.

1723
01:24:47,040 --> 01:24:51,419
‪Someone has to
‪clear this stage eventually.

1724
01:24:51,503 --> 01:24:53,379
‪Even if it's not me,

1725
01:24:53,463 --> 01:24:55,173
‪sharing what I know is the right call.

1726
01:24:55,882 --> 01:24:57,550
‪-This is cool.
‪-So cool.

1727
01:24:57,634 --> 01:24:59,677
‪It feels like I'm reunited
‪with a kidnapped archaeologist.

1728
01:24:59,761 --> 01:25:01,054
‪-Totally.
‪-"Kidnapped archaeologist"?

1729
01:25:01,137 --> 01:25:03,181
‪-What now? Oh, I guess it's time.
‪-Lights out.

1730
01:25:03,264 --> 01:25:04,516
‪-Yeah, lights out.
‪-Okay.

1731
01:25:04,599 --> 01:25:05,809
‪-Look here.
‪-Okay.

1732
01:25:06,351 --> 01:25:07,852
‪-When forming sentences,
‪-Yes?

1733
01:25:07,936 --> 01:25:09,312
‪-a bar on top means it's a noun.
‪-Okay.

1734
01:25:09,395 --> 01:25:11,648
‪-And a dot on top means it's a verb.
‪-Verb, right.

1735
01:25:12,273 --> 01:25:14,484
‪When it's an acute accent…

1736
01:25:14,567 --> 01:25:15,485
‪-Adjective?
‪-That's right.

1737
01:25:15,568 --> 01:25:17,153
‪Like "drinking water."

1738
01:25:17,237 --> 01:25:18,822
‪You pick things up fast.

1739
01:25:18,905 --> 01:25:21,407
‪"Wood plus fire equals charcoal."

1740
01:25:21,491 --> 01:25:23,618
‪So with the two dots, it becomes "black."

1741
01:25:23,701 --> 01:25:25,078
‪In other words, the color of charcoal.

1742
01:25:25,161 --> 01:25:26,830
‪And over here, we have some numbers.

1743
01:25:29,165 --> 01:25:30,250
‪How'd you figure all this out?

1744
01:25:30,333 --> 01:25:31,835
‪-That's incredible.
‪-Isn't it?

1745
01:25:31,918 --> 01:25:34,587
‪-Okay, this is the black hole.
‪-Let's come back here.

1746
01:25:34,671 --> 01:25:39,259
‪All these pictures are here
‪to help us understand these two puzzles.

1747
01:25:39,342 --> 01:25:40,176
‪-That one?
‪-Yeah.

1748
01:25:40,260 --> 01:25:43,054
‪-It was created to teach us this language.
‪-At the end.

1749
01:25:43,138 --> 01:25:45,056
‪These sections
‪are set apart from the rest.

1750
01:25:45,640 --> 01:25:47,183
‪"When the bird calls out six times,

1751
01:25:47,267 --> 01:25:49,310
‪you cover the sun."

1752
01:25:49,394 --> 01:25:50,854
‪Remember "shadow" from over there?

1753
01:25:50,937 --> 01:25:53,356
‪The verb form of it would be "to cover."

1754
01:25:54,232 --> 01:25:55,942
‪That's what we concluded.
‪"You cover the sun."

1755
01:25:56,025 --> 01:25:58,403
‪And "When day turns to night,

1756
01:25:58,486 --> 01:26:00,572
‪you can see the path."

1757
01:26:01,197 --> 01:26:03,825
‪We only found this today.

1758
01:26:03,908 --> 01:26:05,410
‪The bird will call out again
‪tomorrow morning.

1759
01:26:05,493 --> 01:26:07,996
‪Now that we've found this, we're thinking
‪maybe the sun will come down.

1760
01:26:08,079 --> 01:26:10,540
‪-So you need to insert this into that.
‪-Right.

1761
01:26:11,708 --> 01:26:15,712
‪-And what we need to do now is that.
‪-We think that's next.

1762
01:26:15,795 --> 01:26:17,130
‪I assume it started in a jumble.

1763
01:26:17,213 --> 01:26:19,174
‪It was the most random jumble.

1764
01:26:19,257 --> 01:26:22,677
‪We think this place
‪must have its own survival rules,

1765
01:26:22,760 --> 01:26:24,804
‪and we're wondering
‪if we can figure out any other rules.

1766
01:26:24,888 --> 01:26:29,475
‪This is the legacy of everyone
‪who came before me here.

1767
01:26:29,559 --> 01:26:31,644
‪-It's their legacy.
‪-Right, I get it.

1768
01:26:31,728 --> 01:26:34,981
‪And because this legacy must continue
‪even if I get eliminated,

1769
01:26:35,064 --> 01:26:36,649
‪I'm sharing everything I know.

1770
01:26:37,609 --> 01:26:41,821
‪-I feel a sense of purpose now.
‪-I haven't talked this fast in so long.

1771
01:26:41,905 --> 01:26:43,948
‪I think we can solve this
‪if we put our heads together.

1772
01:26:44,032 --> 01:26:45,825
‪-Let's give it our all tomorrow morning.
‪-Sure.

1773
01:26:45,909 --> 01:26:47,911
‪Let's start first thing tomorrow.

1774
01:26:47,994 --> 01:26:49,329
‪I'm gonna sleep now.

1775
01:26:49,412 --> 01:26:53,124
‪-Right, we have to sleep. We're all tired.
‪-Let's get some sleep to recover.

1776
01:26:58,546 --> 01:26:59,589
‪I'm exhausted.

1777
01:27:15,146 --> 01:27:16,606
<i>‪I slept much better than yesterday.</i>

1778
01:27:24,656 --> 01:27:26,074
‪You're working right away?

1779
01:27:26,157 --> 01:27:26,991
‪What?

1780
01:27:27,075 --> 01:27:28,201
‪You're working right away?

1781
01:27:28,284 --> 01:27:29,118
‪Yeah.

1782
01:27:31,621 --> 01:27:34,207
<i>‪I'm sleeping so well here.</i>
<i>‪What's wrong with me?</i>

1783
01:27:35,124 --> 01:27:36,793
<i>‪I felt like I was dying.</i>

1784
01:27:36,876 --> 01:27:38,002
<i>‪It's so incredibly dry.</i>

1785
01:27:38,086 --> 01:27:40,338
<i>‪This is what sleeping in a desert</i>
<i>‪must </i><i>‪feel </i><i>‪like.</i>

1786
01:27:43,675 --> 01:27:47,887
<i>‪The question of whether I can adapt</i>
<i>‪is long past.</i>

1787
01:27:47,971 --> 01:27:49,681
<i>‪You have no choice but to adapt.</i>

1788
01:27:50,348 --> 01:27:51,516
‪Let's do this.

1789
01:27:52,267 --> 01:27:54,394
‪I think we should start from "This place."

1790
01:27:54,894 --> 01:27:57,730
‪There's actually a lot
‪we can change in the upper rows.

1791
01:27:58,231 --> 01:27:59,983
‪Shouldn't it be "There are two methods"?

1792
01:28:01,567 --> 01:28:04,612
‪That's the bird. It'll call out six times.

1793
01:28:05,280 --> 01:28:06,322
‪But this…

1794
01:28:09,242 --> 01:28:11,494
‪It sounds so unsettling.

1795
01:28:11,577 --> 01:28:14,163
‪It's not coming down.
‪We can't put the moon in.

1796
01:28:14,247 --> 01:28:16,749
<i>‪We thought that since we found the moon,</i>

1797
01:28:16,833 --> 01:28:19,627
‪the sun would come down automatically
‪when the bird called out.

1798
01:28:19,711 --> 01:28:21,379
‪But it didn't.

1799
01:28:21,462 --> 01:28:23,548
‪Hold on a second.

1800
01:28:26,551 --> 01:28:29,679
‪"The bird calls out six times."

1801
01:28:29,762 --> 01:28:32,890
‪-"You can cover…"
‪-"Cover the sun."

1802
01:28:33,975 --> 01:28:35,184
‪How do we cover the sun?

1803
01:28:36,227 --> 01:28:37,895
‪How can we make it come down?

1804
01:28:38,396 --> 01:28:40,898
‪Or is there a way for us to go up?

1805
01:28:42,108 --> 01:28:45,570
‪We can insert the moon to cover the sun?

1806
01:28:45,653 --> 01:28:46,612
‪How?

1807
01:28:47,196 --> 01:28:49,240
<i>‪The sun wouldn't come down,</i>
<i>‪and we couldn't go up,</i>

1808
01:28:49,324 --> 01:28:50,616
<i>‪so we needed to send the moon up.</i>

1809
01:28:51,367 --> 01:28:55,747
<i>‪I had a feeling we'd find something</i>
<i>‪if we looked carefully enough.</i>

1810
01:28:56,539 --> 01:28:58,624
<i>‪So I inspected everything</i>

1811
01:28:58,708 --> 01:29:03,713
<i>‪and discovered a pole that looked</i>
<i>‪a little different from the others.</i>

1812
01:29:13,306 --> 01:29:14,515
‪Why does this come out?

1813
01:29:14,599 --> 01:29:16,017
‪Do some of them just come out?

1814
01:29:16,642 --> 01:29:17,977
‪-Hang on.
‪-That's it.

1815
01:29:18,061 --> 01:29:20,563
‪Oh my gosh. This is it.
‪You can stick that in here.

1816
01:29:20,646 --> 01:29:23,274
‪That was a total escape room approach.

1817
01:29:23,358 --> 01:29:25,777
‪-There's a slot here.
‪-No way.

1818
01:29:25,860 --> 01:29:27,111
‪Where was that?

1819
01:29:27,612 --> 01:29:29,405
‪There was something like that there?

1820
01:29:29,489 --> 01:29:32,992
<i>‪I've been here for 24 hours.</i>
<i>‪How did I miss it?</i>

1821
01:29:33,076 --> 01:29:34,827
‪So we could've done this yesterday.

1822
01:29:34,911 --> 01:29:38,122
‪-Every new person discovers something.
‪-I know, right?

1823
01:29:38,206 --> 01:29:43,002
‪I never would've imagined
‪that there was something in the fence.

1824
01:29:44,754 --> 01:29:46,589
‪Eureka. Seriously.

1825
01:29:47,173 --> 01:29:48,758
‪Guys, this is amazing.

1826
01:29:49,550 --> 01:29:51,594
‪-Collective intelligence is important.
‪-It really is.

1827
01:29:51,677 --> 01:29:53,513
‪-Are we supposed to cover that?
‪-I think so.

1828
01:29:53,596 --> 01:29:54,931
‪-Just like this?
‪-Yeah.

1829
01:29:55,014 --> 01:29:56,849
‪Will something happen when we cover it?

1830
01:29:56,933 --> 01:29:58,142
‪Should I give it a go?

1831
01:29:59,143 --> 01:30:00,186
‪Hold on.

1832
01:30:08,236 --> 01:30:09,278
‪Like this?

1833
01:30:10,154 --> 01:30:11,364
‪Is this how we do it?

1834
01:30:12,490 --> 01:30:13,491
‪Or create a shadow?

1835
01:30:13,991 --> 01:30:15,827
‪-Is this right?
‪-Maybe the other side?

1836
01:30:16,410 --> 01:30:17,328
‪The other side?

1837
01:30:24,585 --> 01:30:25,503
‪That's not it.

1838
01:30:26,212 --> 01:30:28,798
<i>‪We tried covering it with the moon,</i>
<i>‪but nothing happened.</i>

1839
01:30:28,881 --> 01:30:30,424
‪Now we have to think again.

1840
01:30:30,508 --> 01:30:31,467
‪What could it be?

1841
01:30:32,135 --> 01:30:33,344
‪Maybe here?

1842
01:30:39,684 --> 01:30:41,894
‪Where are we supposed to hold this up to?

1843
01:30:47,900 --> 01:30:51,154
‪So do we have to cover the sun and wait?

1844
01:30:51,237 --> 01:30:53,239
‪While holding the pole up like that?

1845
01:30:53,865 --> 01:30:55,825
‪What is that, a magnifying glass?

1846
01:30:56,784 --> 01:31:00,454
‪That alone
‪doesn't seem to trigger anything.

1847
01:31:01,164 --> 01:31:02,248
‪Or maybe

1848
01:31:03,040 --> 01:31:05,042
‪we need to do it the exact moment
‪the bird calls out.

1849
01:31:05,668 --> 01:31:06,836
‪-So it's about timing?
‪-Yeah.

1850
01:31:06,919 --> 01:31:08,880
‪"When the bird calls out,

1851
01:31:08,963 --> 01:31:10,798
‪you cover the sun."

1852
01:31:10,882 --> 01:31:12,300
‪I think that's what it says.

1853
01:31:12,800 --> 01:31:15,887
‪Perhaps we need to go and cover it
‪the moment the bird calls out.

1854
01:31:17,722 --> 01:31:19,807
‪-We're too late.
‪-Right, we missed the window.

1855
01:31:19,891 --> 01:31:25,313
‪There must be some condition
‪for when the bird calls out.

1856
01:31:25,396 --> 01:31:28,357
‪How long after the lights come on
‪does the bird call?

1857
01:31:28,441 --> 01:31:30,693
‪About 30 minutes?

1858
01:31:33,404 --> 01:31:34,238
‪What?

1859
01:31:36,073 --> 01:31:38,743
‪After the lights come on, we can measure
‪the time with the hourglass.

1860
01:31:39,577 --> 01:31:40,578
‪Yeah.

1861
01:31:41,204 --> 01:31:44,040
‪So you're saying
‪it's roughly about 30 minutes.

1862
01:31:44,123 --> 01:31:46,125
‪-So run the 15-minute one twice?
‪-Yeah.

1863
01:31:46,209 --> 01:31:48,044
‪Or it could even be 15 minutes.

1864
01:31:48,753 --> 01:31:49,879
‪And then what?

1865
01:31:49,962 --> 01:31:51,672
‪-After that…
‪-We can track when the bird calls out.

1866
01:31:51,756 --> 01:31:52,924
‪We'll know when it calls out.

1867
01:31:53,007 --> 01:31:55,384
‪-So we'll know when it's coming.
‪-Yeah.

1868
01:31:55,468 --> 01:31:57,136
‪So if we know roughly when it calls out,

1869
01:31:57,220 --> 01:32:00,389
‪we can be on standby
‪around the time the hourglass runs out

1870
01:32:00,473 --> 01:32:02,558
‪and cover the sun as soon as it calls out.

1871
01:32:02,642 --> 01:32:04,185
‪So we lost our chance today, right?

1872
01:32:04,268 --> 01:32:05,228
‪Yeah.

1873
01:32:07,271 --> 01:32:08,147
‪Gone.

1874
01:32:08,231 --> 01:32:09,273
‪-It's gone?
‪-Yeah.

1875
01:32:09,857 --> 01:32:12,526
‪We should be able to do it for sure
‪tomorrow morning.

1876
01:32:12,610 --> 01:32:13,444
‪Now we know.

1877
01:32:13,527 --> 01:32:15,321
‪We should've done it
‪when the bird called out.

1878
01:32:15,404 --> 01:32:17,198
‪If only we'd found the pole earlier.

1879
01:32:17,281 --> 01:32:19,992
‪-Is there any way to make it call out?
‪-That's really disappointing.

1880
01:32:20,576 --> 01:32:21,953
‪What could this game be?

1881
01:32:22,036 --> 01:32:24,622
‪We need to figure this out
‪before we can do anything over there.

1882
01:32:26,457 --> 01:32:27,750
‪Ancient hieroglyph users…

1883
01:32:29,877 --> 01:32:31,963
‪Let's channel
‪our inner ancient civilization.

1884
01:32:33,172 --> 01:32:34,340
‪I'm so bored.

1885
01:32:34,423 --> 01:32:36,550
‪I want to play a game.
‪What's this game they made?

1886
01:32:36,634 --> 01:32:38,261
‪Hey, Stella.

1887
01:32:38,344 --> 01:32:39,512
‪Aren't you so bored these days?

1888
01:32:42,056 --> 01:32:44,308
‪This place drives everyone mad.

1889
01:32:44,392 --> 01:32:46,477
‪Shall we devise an amusing game?

1890
01:32:47,728 --> 01:32:49,105
‪But no matter how I look at it,

1891
01:32:50,106 --> 01:32:54,193
‪that fits perfectly,
‪so whatever we do probably involves that.

1892
01:32:54,277 --> 01:32:57,029
‪Right, it can't just be here
‪for no reason.

1893
01:32:57,655 --> 01:32:58,489
‪Should we try?

1894
01:32:58,572 --> 01:33:00,283
‪-I think it might be better that we do.
‪-Yeah.

1895
01:33:00,366 --> 01:33:02,118
‪Let's get all the Korean sorted out first.

1896
01:33:06,038 --> 01:33:08,124
<i>‪We were only combining the Korean,</i>

1897
01:33:08,207 --> 01:33:10,334
<i>‪but there were </i><i>‪more </i><i>‪characters</i>
<i>‪on the back,</i>

1898
01:33:10,418 --> 01:33:14,964
‪and those characters matched
‪the hieroglyphs on the other pictures.

1899
01:33:15,047 --> 01:33:17,800
<i>‪So I thought </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪backside</i>
<i>‪might form sentences too.</i>

1900
01:33:17,883 --> 01:33:19,802
‪Have you tried flipping all of them over

1901
01:33:19,885 --> 01:33:22,013
‪in this current formation?

1902
01:33:22,096 --> 01:33:22,930
‪No, not yet.

1903
01:33:27,768 --> 01:33:29,562
‪-This goes on top, right?
‪-Right.

1904
01:33:29,645 --> 01:33:32,148
‪So we flip it like this
‪if we're supposed to flip it.

1905
01:33:32,732 --> 01:33:34,483
‪Is this "person"?

1906
01:33:34,567 --> 01:33:36,360
‪-No, wait. What's this?
‪-This one? What's this?

1907
01:33:36,444 --> 01:33:37,987
‪-Hey, what's this?
‪-That's "and."

1908
01:33:38,070 --> 01:33:41,324
‪-"And"?
‪-Then it wouldn't go at the very front.

1909
01:33:41,907 --> 01:33:43,159
‪-Right.
‪-Yeah.

1910
01:33:43,242 --> 01:33:44,827
‪Then that would be the wrong spot.

1911
01:33:44,910 --> 01:33:45,995
‪Could be.

1912
01:33:46,078 --> 01:33:47,830
‪So what are we sure about here?

1913
01:33:47,913 --> 01:33:50,916
‪"Final match" and "second."

1914
01:33:51,000 --> 01:33:52,043
‪-You're sure?
‪-Yeah.

1915
01:33:52,126 --> 01:33:54,128
‪Let me flip this over.

1916
01:33:59,550 --> 01:34:00,468
‪That fits.

1917
01:34:00,551 --> 01:34:01,427
‪It's coming together.

1918
01:34:01,510 --> 01:34:03,512
‪But you know what's weird?

1919
01:34:03,596 --> 01:34:05,848
‪There are 12 rows here.

1920
01:34:05,931 --> 01:34:07,224
‪-Twelve rows.
‪-Okay.

1921
01:34:07,308 --> 01:34:12,229
‪We have one for the marker on top
‪and one for the character itself.

1922
01:34:12,313 --> 01:34:14,148
‪The spacing lines up perfectly.

1923
01:34:14,231 --> 01:34:16,233
‪-So let's do this.
‪-You're right.

1924
01:34:16,317 --> 01:34:18,861
‪-See these part-of-speech markers?
‪-Yeah.

1925
01:34:18,944 --> 01:34:20,863
‪Let's make sure they only appear
‪in odd-numbered rows

1926
01:34:20,946 --> 01:34:22,365
‪-when seen from above.
‪-Right.

1927
01:34:24,658 --> 01:34:27,328
‪That's why I think we have 12 rows
‪when we just have 11 columns.

1928
01:34:27,411 --> 01:34:29,497
‪Things are finally coming together.

1929
01:34:29,580 --> 01:34:31,082
‪This is so fun.

1930
01:34:31,165 --> 01:34:31,999
‪It is.

1931
01:34:32,083 --> 01:34:33,250
‪-It's fun.
‪-It is.

1932
01:34:33,334 --> 01:34:35,336
‪-Collective intelligence!
‪-Excellent.

1933
01:34:35,419 --> 01:34:38,339
‪We figured that the odd rows
‪hold the part-of-speech markers,

1934
01:34:38,422 --> 01:34:44,387
‪and the even rows hold the characters
‪that express meaning.

1935
01:34:44,470 --> 01:34:46,722
<i>‪Things started clicking into place.</i>

1936
01:34:46,806 --> 01:34:49,392
‪Should we pull out all the even-row

1937
01:34:49,475 --> 01:34:51,644
‪-Separate them?
‪-and odd-row characters?

1938
01:34:51,727 --> 01:34:53,562
‪-That's a good idea.
‪-Sounds good.

1939
01:34:53,646 --> 01:34:54,939
‪Should we put them here?

1940
01:34:55,022 --> 01:34:56,065
‪Let's put odd-row ones here.

1941
01:34:56,148 --> 01:34:58,943
‪-Yeah, odd-row.
‪-Empty ones could be either, right?

1942
01:34:59,026 --> 01:35:00,111
‪Yeah, they could be.

1943
01:35:00,194 --> 01:35:01,570
‪Should we separate the empty ones?

1944
01:35:01,654 --> 01:35:03,197
‪-Yeah, let's do that.
‪-Okay.

1945
01:35:03,280 --> 01:35:04,490
‪I'll put the empty ones down here.

1946
01:35:04,573 --> 01:35:05,825
‪-Odd-row ones here, right?
‪-Down there?

1947
01:35:05,908 --> 01:35:07,243
‪-Odd, even, empty.
‪-Odd, even…

1948
01:35:07,326 --> 01:35:08,452
‪-Even here?
‪-Yes.

1949
01:35:13,541 --> 01:35:14,750
‪This is great.

1950
01:35:14,834 --> 01:35:17,420
‪If you look at the preexisting text,

1951
01:35:17,503 --> 01:35:19,713
‪you can see there are no spaces,
‪and the end is blank.

1952
01:35:19,797 --> 01:35:22,007
‪Sentences are written left to right,

1953
01:35:22,091 --> 01:35:23,926
‪so the left side is always filled.

1954
01:35:24,009 --> 01:35:26,512
‪The right side might be empty,

1955
01:35:26,595 --> 01:35:28,722
‪but if the sentence fills the whole row,
‪it might not be.

1956
01:35:28,806 --> 01:35:30,474
‪Bottom line is
‪there could be empty spaces.

1957
01:35:30,558 --> 01:35:32,476
‪This is the first column, right?

1958
01:35:32,560 --> 01:35:34,937
‪I don't think the first column
‪would have empty spaces.

1959
01:35:35,020 --> 01:35:39,316
‪I think all the hieroglyphs
‪will be clustered on this side.

1960
01:35:40,860 --> 01:35:42,695
‪I think from here to here…

1961
01:35:42,778 --> 01:35:44,822
‪-Definitely right?
‪-Yeah.

1962
01:35:44,905 --> 01:35:47,908
‪Why don't we flip it
‪and see what it says first?

1963
01:35:47,992 --> 01:35:49,034
‪This one? Okay.

1964
01:35:51,370 --> 01:35:52,329
‪Wait, isn't this "six"?

1965
01:35:52,413 --> 01:35:54,039
‪Right. "Second," "sixth…"

1966
01:35:54,123 --> 01:35:55,708
‪"Second, on the sixth day…"

1967
01:35:57,460 --> 01:35:59,295
‪-"Second, on the sixth day…"
‪-I think that's right.

1968
01:35:59,378 --> 01:36:02,089
‪We have "Second, on the sixth day"
‪right over here.

1969
01:36:02,173 --> 01:36:03,340
‪-The characters say it.
‪-Right.

1970
01:36:03,424 --> 01:36:05,468
‪"Second, on the sixth day…"

1971
01:36:05,551 --> 01:36:08,262
‪We assumed "X happens to cause Y"
‪would come after this.

1972
01:36:08,345 --> 01:36:09,930
‪-We have "second" here.
‪-Right.

1973
01:36:10,806 --> 01:36:12,850
‪-"On the sixth day."
‪-Yeah.

1974
01:36:12,933 --> 01:36:13,934
‪Unbelievable.

1975
01:36:14,018 --> 01:36:16,145
‪So the messages match?

1976
01:36:16,228 --> 01:36:19,023
‪There's a sort of echo happening
‪between the texts in both languages.

1977
01:36:19,106 --> 01:36:20,774
‪They wrote in their language,

1978
01:36:20,858 --> 01:36:22,776
‪but if you flip it over,
‪you get the Korean version.

1979
01:36:22,860 --> 01:36:25,821
‪When we assemble it in Korean and flip it,
‪we get a version in their language.

1980
01:36:25,905 --> 01:36:27,573
‪-Just like a translator.
‪-Yeah.

1981
01:36:27,656 --> 01:36:28,949
‪-This is a translator.
‪-Yeah.

1982
01:36:29,033 --> 01:36:32,661
‪So this board is a translator,
‪and we took it apart.

1983
01:36:32,745 --> 01:36:33,871
‪That sounds right.

1984
01:36:33,954 --> 01:36:37,082
‪If we arrange it in Korean and flip it,
‪we get the language of the exile zone.

1985
01:36:37,166 --> 01:36:39,835
‪If we arrange it in the language
‪of the exile zone and flip it,

1986
01:36:39,919 --> 01:36:40,920
‪we get it in Korean.

1987
01:36:41,003 --> 01:36:42,421
‪That's what we figured out.

1988
01:36:42,505 --> 01:36:44,131
‪But if you look at it,

1989
01:36:44,215 --> 01:36:47,551
‪"Second, on the sixth day" in Korean is
‪two rows above its exile language version.

1990
01:36:47,635 --> 01:36:49,303
‪It's sitting too low,

1991
01:36:49,386 --> 01:36:52,056
‪so I don't think the characters
‪on each side are an exact match.

1992
01:36:52,139 --> 01:36:54,391
‪So the characters on each side
‪don't match 100%?

1993
01:36:54,475 --> 01:36:57,061
‪We need so many characters
‪for the same phrase in Korean,

1994
01:36:57,144 --> 01:36:58,521
‪whereas in this language,
‪it ends in three characters.

1995
01:36:58,604 --> 01:37:00,022
‪You're right.

1996
01:37:00,105 --> 01:37:02,775
‪-We've figured out quite a lot though.
‪-I think we can do this.

1997
01:37:03,275 --> 01:37:06,695
‪I moved it down to save space for now.

1998
01:37:06,779 --> 01:37:09,657
‪This part seems right. Because here--

1999
01:37:09,740 --> 01:37:11,242
‪-"If you win…"
‪-"If you win…"

2000
01:37:11,325 --> 01:37:13,452
‪-That's incredible.
‪-Okay.

2001
01:37:13,536 --> 01:37:17,122
‪-This line here has the markers.
‪-Okay.

2002
01:37:17,206 --> 01:37:20,793
‪We need <i>‪ri</i>‪ for <i>‪seungri,</i>‪ as in "to win,"
‪and there's only one in this entire set.

2003
01:37:20,876 --> 01:37:22,545
‪Wait, but what about that one over there?

2004
01:37:22,628 --> 01:37:23,629
‪-Where?
‪-There is.

2005
01:37:23,712 --> 01:37:25,589
‪Here it is.

2006
01:37:25,673 --> 01:37:27,800
‪-But this <i>‪ri</i>‪ doesn't fit.
‪-It doesn't.

2007
01:37:27,883 --> 01:37:29,927
‪-This isn't the right one for over here.
‪-Yeah.

2008
01:37:30,719 --> 01:37:33,722
‪We finally know enough to know
‪what fits and what doesn't.

2009
01:37:33,806 --> 01:37:36,392
‪It's all connected.

2010
01:37:36,475 --> 01:37:37,810
‪Well done, production team.

2011
01:37:41,605 --> 01:37:44,400
‪I can't believe I thought
‪I could solve this purely in Korean.

2012
01:37:44,483 --> 01:37:45,693
‪How foolish.

